&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p class="powerpress_links powerpress_subscribe_links"&gt;
  Subscribe: &lt;a href="https://itunes.apple.com/WebObjects/MZStore.woa/wa/viewPodcast?id=301670981&amp;amp;mt=2&amp;amp;ls=1#episodeGuid=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.bitcoin.kn%2F%3Fp%3D1887" class="powerpress_link_subscribe powerpress_link_subscribe_itunes" title="Subscribe on Apple Podcasts" rel="nofollow"&gt;Apple Podcasts&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href="https://subscribeonandroid.com/www.bitcoin.kn/feed/podcast/" class="powerpress_link_subscribe powerpress_link_subscribe_android" title="Subscribe on Android" rel="nofollow"&gt;Android&lt;/a&gt; | &lt;a href="https://www.bitcoin.kn/feed/podcast/" class="powerpress_link_subscribe powerpress_link_subscribe_rss" title="Subscribe via RSS" rel="nofollow"&gt;RSS&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;!-- Keep this code as is --&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.trace.com/"&gt;Trace Mayer&lt;/a&gt; joins Cedric Youngelman on the Bitcoin Matrix Podcast, sharing his origin story from playing text-based online games and experimenting with digital gold currencies in the mid-90s to discovering Bitcoin through deep study of Austrian economics and monetary law in law school. They explore the hidden history of money in American law, the significance of Dr. Edwin Vieira's Pieces of Eight, and how GATA exposed central bank gold price suppression. The conversation digs into Trace's pioneering role in Bitcoin -- from launching Run to Gold in 2008 and funding Kraken and Armory to coining the stock-to-flow concept for Bitcoin -- and his conviction that monetary sovereignty is worth fighting for despite intimidation from those who control the existing financial system.
&lt;p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Resources&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.runtogold.com/"&gt;Run to Gold&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.goldmoney.com/"&gt;Goldmoney&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.gata.org/"&gt;GATA&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.runtogold.com/pieces-of-eight/"&gt;Pieces of Eight&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TCU-soMs1wY"&gt;Network Effects&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Show Notes&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Rise of Bitcoin and Institutional Adoption - 0:00 - 2:34&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trace Mayer’s Journey into Bitcoin - 2:35 - 12:43&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding Monetary Sovereignty and Gold -  12:44 - 20:05&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Transition from Gold to Bitcoin -  20:06 - 28:40&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Economics of Violence and Digital Scarcity -  28:41 - 31:59&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time Preference and Family Dynamics in Economics -  32:00 - 39:11&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gold’s Role in the Modern Economy -  39:12 - 42:23&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wealth Creation and Institutional Adoption of Bitcoin -  42:24 - 43:12&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Block Size Wars: A Peaceful Secession -  43:13 - 46:20&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Key Influences in Bitcoin’s Development -  46:21 - 55:10&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bitcoin as a Store of Value -  55:11 - 58:34&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proof of Keys: Flexing M...

